{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1282242-question-on-call-lightning","id":1282242,"title":"Question on Call Lightning","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-22T19:31:32-08:00","id":1282242,"title":"Question on Call Lightning","content":"So I was looking at the Forces 3-dot spell Call Lightning and I was wanting some clarification. According to the spell, It does damage according <br /> to the Electricity rules on page 244 and the damage is unavoidable. Those rules state that electricity is bashing damage and a Lightning Bolt is 10 Bashing. The Spell's Primary Spell Factor is Potency. Since Potency determines the damage value of Spells my question is does the Spell Potency stack on top of the 10 damage a lightning bolt does on it's own?<br /> <br /> Not that I am complaining in regards to this, I mean you have to have a Storm in the first place in order to cast this spell, and if you are indoors the lighting can't hit them and just like in previous version of Mage, this is not a spell you should be able to cast multiple times in a row without invoking some Paradox is there are Sleeper's present and Mage is a game where your characters are pretty OP coming out of the gate, but I just wanted to get some clarification for my own piece of mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24927-wodstoryteller","name":"WoDStoryteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T20:00:39-08:00","id":1282245,"title":"","content":"Potency determines the damage value of 